## 5. Set Up Browserless Tests with Spring Boot
----
Framework: common
Heading: Access Session-Scoped Beans
Document Path: v25.3/building-apps/testing/browserless/setup-spring-boot.md (use get_full_document to get complete context)
----

This example assumes a session-scoped `Cart` service and a `CartView` whose **Add to cart** button adds an item to the cart.
The provider resolves the bean for the user whose window is active --- here the only window, which the preceding `navigate()` call used.
Each test has a user of its own, so each test gets an empty cart.
In a test with several users, call `activate()` on a window of the intended user before resolving the bean.
The same approach works for a bean with Spring's `@SessionScope`, which can also be injected directly.
See [Spring Session-Scoped Beans](v25.3/flow/testing/browserless/environment-differences.md) for scope guarantees and other deferred-lookup options.

